  "notes": "Every case must pass. 'cell' is the type the value arrives as from the Sheets API (date = a real date cell, text = a string). Numeric dates are always day-first (India). Year inference when the year is missing: if a weekday is present, pick the year in {today.year-1, today.year, today.year+1} whose date falls on that weekday, choosing the one closest to today; if none match, the value is invalid. Without a weekday, pick the year that puts the date within 6 months either side of today. endDateCases (PRD 6.3.4, N64 to N67) read a Date together with an End date column, same reference today. end null means the tracker maps no End date column; an empty End date leaves the Date alone. With an End date filled, the Date must be one date (blank: end_without_start; a window or open date: start_not_single; invalid: its own reason) and the End date one date in a single form (else end_date_unreadable). Years follow N36 for the pair: a real date cell has its year; the side with a year is read first and the other takes its year around it, else the only side with a weekday, else the End date. An End date before its Date is range_end_before_start (Fri 17 Oct around a real 13 Oct 2026 reads 17 Oct 2025); the same day is single; a later day is a window.",
